  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 259 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge of high pressure will remain centered over\nthe plains Sunday into early next week. Highs in the 90s to\nnear 100 degrees are expected Sunday through Tuesday with daily\nafternoon/early evening heat index values in the 100 to 110\nrange expected. A Heat Advisory is in effect from 1 pm this\nafternoon through 7 PM Tuesday. \n\nOverall dry conditions are expected Sunday through Tuesday as a\ncap remains in place across the region. \n\nThe ensemble model members show the upper level ridge pushing\nback to the west some during the middle to end of next week.\nThis could bring temperatures but to near normal for this time\nof year with highs in the upper 80s to the middle 90s. An upper\nlevel disturbance will move around the upper level ridge and\ncould bring some shower and thunderstorm chances to the region\nlate next week, but there is still uncertainty on the timing and\ntrack of the system, on just how far south it can track.",
